  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nDiurnal cu dissipated prior to sunset with slackening winds. Surface\nhigh pressure will drift east across the region through tonight and \nbe centered over eastern Ohio by Sunday morning. With clearing skies \nand light winds, expect good radiational cooling tonight with \nwidespread frost and some sub-freezing temperature. Generally expect \nlows in the upper 20s to lower 30s, but even cooler readings will be \npossible in outlying/sheltered areas. A Freeze Warning remains in \neffect for tonight into Sunday morning to account for this.\n\nOtherwise, dry conditions will prevail through next week as the \nsurface high remains in place across much of the Great Lakes region. \nExpect a gradual warming trend through midweek as the airmass slowly \nmoderates.",
